## Phase E: Curriculum Learning (Design Only)

**Concept:** Train on high-quality segments first, then gradually add lower-quality ones.

**Implementation in [08_train_bart_summarizer.py](file:///d:/Users/Mihir/Downloads/Documents/Mihir%20Codes/Dp_Project/scripts/text_processing/08_train_bart_summarizer.py):**

```python
# In the train() method, after loading data:

# Split training data by quality
high_quality = [s for s in train_ds.samples 
                if s.get('quality_score', 0) > 0.6 
                and s.get('entity_coverage', 0) > 0.5]
remaining = [s for s in train_ds.samples if s not in high_quality]

curriculum_switch_epoch = 3  # Switch to full data after 3 epochs

for epoch in range(1, self.epochs + 1):
    if epoch <= curriculum_switch_epoch:
        # Phase 1: train on high-quality only
        current_samples = high_quality
        self.logger.info(f"Curriculum: using {len(high_quality)} high-quality samples")
    else:
        # Phase 2: train on ALL samples
        current_samples = train_ds.samples
        self.logger.info(f"Curriculum: using ALL {len(train_ds.samples)} samples")
    
    # Create DataLoader with current_samples
    curr_ds = LectureSummarizationDataset(current_samples, tokenizer, ...)
    train_loader = DataLoader(curr_ds, ...)
```

**Why it helps:** Prevents the model from memorizing noisy/low-quality pseudo-summaries in early epochs when it's most sensitive. By the time all data is introduced, the model has learned a good prior for summarization.

